kintanji brown jackson grew up in a  middle-class suburb of miami where both  parents worked as school teachers and  where she made a name for herself at  debate competitions by writing her name  kentunji on the chalkboard for all to  see she would have to  um  speak before  largely white audiences and had to sort  of  bridge that gap and convey to them  instantaneously in case there was any  subtle bias or just  lack of familiarity with her just  starting from her name steven rosenthal  was jackson's classmate from an early  age he says he never doubted that one  day his charismatic friend would achieve  these heights so she just drew people  toward her  and  people wanted to support her and um  respected her so she just had  all the tools in addition to being  brilliant  to succeed in whatever she chose to do  jackson has been a federal judge for  nine years and currently sits on the d.c  court of appeals she's issued about 500  opinions but none on the hot button  issues of abortion gun rights and  freedom of religion  she did gain fame in 2019 when she  blocked president trump from shielding  former white house counsel dom again  from testifying before congress writing  presidents are not kings  judge jackson deserves to be confirmed  as the next justice supreme court some  republicans have accused jackson of  being the favored choice of far left  groups but the same senate confirmed her  to her appeals court position a year ago  with support from three republicans  jackson would replace another liberal  stephen breyer the justice she once  clerked for and she would be the first  black woman to join the u.s supreme  court  i can only hope that my life and career  my love of this country and the  constitution  and my commitment to upholding the rule  of law and the sacred principles upon  which this great nation was founded will  inspire future generations  of americans even me when i think about  myself as a as a lawyer i didn't have  many um people to look up to that looked  like i did and so i think for young um  girls to be able to  look at justice jackson and see where  she is and and how far she's come is  really really going to be an important  moment jackson has seen her future  clearly since high school telling a  yearbook editor she wanted to go into  law and eventually have a judicial  appointment  now on the brink of being appointed to  the highest court in the land she's also  serving as inspiration for many  heidi joe castro al jazeera washington
 

